    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by elite offensive potential, led by **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) and **Josh Naylor** (77.77). **Corbin Carroll** is our strongest play; he draws a favorable matchup against Littell and benefits from an 8% boost for hitting out of the two-hole, making him the primary driver for our SB and R production despite a minor drag from Littell's control over the run game. **Josh Naylor** similarly thrives against Montero, utilizing a 5% park factor boost and favorable winds to elevate his scoring profile. **Brice Turang** (75.06) and **James Wood** (73.03) are also high-leverage starts today, with **Brice Turang** capitalizing on a significant 14% park boost and wind support, while **James Wood** brings elite xwOBA metrics to a matchup where he faces the slightly vulnerable Rodriguez, L. \n\nRegarding roster construction, the most difficult decision was keeping **Austin Riley** (46.15) on the bench. While his talent floor is high, his matchup against Ashcraft, B\u2014a pitcher with a 3.32 xERA\u2014suppressed his efficiency relative to the rest of the lineup. The optimizer favored **Gabriel Moreno** (71.17) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.05) due to superior platoon splits and softer SP matchups, ultimately pushing **Austin Riley** out of the starting nine. We continue to monitor the status of **Mickey Moniak** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth as we look for production from secondary options like **Alex Freeland** and **Travis Bazzana**.\n\nThe primary risk today involves the volatile SP xERA figures for starters like Ryan and Suarez, which introduced significant variance into our daily projections for **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Jose Caballero**. While **Jose Caballero** maintains a strong 63.52 score, his matchup against a lefty like Suarez requires careful observation, as his platoon advantage is partially offset by the high-efficiency holding profile of the opposing battery. We are proceeding with the current configuration, banking on the speed-heavy profiles of **Brice Turang** and **Corbin Carroll** to provide the separation needed in the SB category.",
